whisper: Lesson 9: A game
whisper:
whisper: Time to open a window. This is a tiny game: move the orange ball with the arrow keys.
whisper: Press F5 and have a go. Close the window when you're done.
whisper:
whisper: The loop goes round about 60 times a second. Each time it checks the keys, wipes the window
whisper: ("consume the window"), draws the ball, then shows the new picture ("reveal the frame").
whisper:
whisper: Your turn. Pick one, or do all of them:
whisper:   make the ball faster
whisper:   change the colours
whisper:   make space put the ball back in the middle

genesis:
  open a world with "Ball", 600, 400
  set across to 300
  set down to 200
  as long as the world lives:
    if key held "left": set across to across minus 5
    if key held "right": set across to across plus 5
    if key held "up": set down to down minus 5
    if key held "down": set down to down plus 5
    consume the window with "black"
    etch a circle with across, down, 20, "orange"
    reveal the frame
and the universe said i love you
